silm:instances_papers_10_graph_knowledge_graph_category_chapters_02_free_category_monad_sections_04_mittens_in_the_monad_concrete_anchors__anchor_j_mittens_index_category a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The shape of the Mittens cocone. Objects: type, evidence, taxonomy, quality, measurement, microchip, process. Arrows include any compatibility-condition arrows between legs (e.g., the taxonomy leg and the type leg both target into D_Mittens but at distinct source vertices). " .
silm:instances_papers_10_graph_knowledge_graph_category_chapters_02_free_category_monad_sections_04_mittens_in_the_monad_concrete_anchors__anchor_d_mittensj_source_diagram_object_at_index_j a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "j=type yields DomesticCat with arrow rdf:type; j=evidence yields VetRecord77 with arrow is_about; j=taxonomy yields the row Felis catus / TSN 183798 with the taxonomy source arrow; j=quality yields BodyMassQuality77 with arrow bearer_of; j=microchip yields MicrochipIdentifier9 with arrow has_microchip. " .
silm:instances_papers_10_graph_knowledge_graph_category_chapters_02_free_category_monad_sections_04_mittens_in_the_monad_concrete_anchors__anchor_lambda_j_cocone_leg_j a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "lambda_type : DomesticCat -> Mittens is the rdf:type arrow read backwards (Mittens is_a DomesticCat). lambda_evidence : VetRecord77 -> Mittens is the is_about arrow. Each lambda_j is an equivalence class of paths in C_G (after equiv_E quotient). " .
silm:instances_papers_10_graph_knowledge_graph_category_chapters_02_free_category_monad_sections_04_mittens_in_the_monad_concrete_anchors__anchor_x_competing_cocone_target a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "X = VetCarePlan22, the clinical-summary node Dr Osei created after the examination visit. The cocone (mu_j) maps each leg object to its contribution to the care plan: mu_type collects species-level care; mu_evidence pulls the recent record; etc. " .
silm:instances_papers_10_graph_knowledge_graph_category_chapters_02_free_category_monad_sections_04_mittens_in_the_monad_concrete_anchors__anchor_u_unique_mediator a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "u : Mittens -> VetCarePlan22 is the unique morphism that factors the care-plan cocone through Mittens. Its uniqueness says: the care plan derives FROM Mittens, and no other cat could play the role. " .
silm:instances_papers_10_graph_knowledge_graph_category_chapters_02_free_category_monad_sections_04_mittens_in_the_monad_concrete_anchors__anchor_tg__g_where_the_colimit_does_not_live a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "T(G) is the underlying graph of Free(G); it has no composition, so colimits don't exist there. G itself has no equation structure, so two paths to the same node need not be identifiable. Only after q : Free(G) -> C_G quotients by equiv_E does the colimit acquire universal force. " .
